          "distinct": true,
          "id": "7ce1b37c9bbd24a61fdab2df37ac73ff0daa43a4",
          "message": "feat(orchestration): Phase 3-A — dispatch planner (dry-run) [OPUS-4.8] (#2286)\n\nCompose the merged readiness engine (#2284) + route resolver (#2283) into a\npure, read-only dispatch planner. `plan_dispatch(ready, routing_doc)` walks the\nconflict-free, priority-ordered ready frontier, resolves each issue's route, and\nemits {number, priority, package, role, model_chain, agent, escalate}.\n\nDry-run only: it does NOT claim an account and does NOT trigger a worker. Those\ntwo credential-gated seams live in `claim_and_dispatch`, which raises\nNotImplementedError pending the maintainer's broker/token-placement sign-off and\nthe automation identity (REGISTRY_ADMIN_TOKEN). Fail-closed: an unresolvable\nroute is flagged role=None/agent=None, never guessed.\n\nCo-authored-by: GPT-5.6 <noreply@openai.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-14T05:07:09Z",
